DING GTK 3: skip unmapped focus targets.

The retained v85 GTK 3 implementation manually reactivates windows after
map/destroy/Overview events. A GTK window can already appear in the tab
list with an actor while still being unmapped. Main.activateWindow() then
triggers Mutter's stack_position >= 0 assertion. Checking only for a
non-null actor does not prevent this.

Apply the same mapped-actor rule to regular windows and desktop fallback.
The existing map event refreshes focus once the window is ready. This
keeps the GTK 3 package and its dependency policy; newer GTK 4 upstream
releases use a different desktop-window implementation.

Upstream component: https://gitlab.com/rastersoft/desktop-icons-ng

--- a/emulateX11WindowType.js
+++ b/emulateX11WindowType.js
@@ -407,6 +407,12 @@
                         let windows = global.display.get_tab_list(Meta.TabList.NORMAL_ALL, global.workspace_manager.get_active_workspace());
                         let anyActive = false;
                         for (let window of windows) {
+                            // A tab-list entry can precede the actor's first mapping.
+                            // Activating it then raises a window outside Mutter's
+                            // stack. Let the existing map callback refresh it later.
+                            if (!window.get_compositor_private()?.mapped) {
+                                continue;
+                            }
                             if ((!window.customJS_ding || !window.customJS_ding._keepAtBottom) && !window.minimized) {
                                 Main.activateWindow(window);
                                 anyActive = true;
@@ -415,6 +421,10 @@
                         }
                         if (!anyActive) {
                             for (let window of this._windowList) {
+                                // The desktop fallback needs the same readiness rule.
+                                if (!window.get_compositor_private()?.mapped) {
+                                    continue;
+                                }
                                 if (window.customJS_ding && window.customJS_ding._keepAtBottom && !window.minimized) {
                                     Main.activateWindow(window);
                                     break;
